# Breaking Games: Holiday Game Plan Dashboard

**Author:** Selena Chik
**Program:** SQL & Database Architecture Externship, Breaking Games

A one-page KPI dashboard summarizing my analysis of Breaking Games' Shopify sales, marketing channels, and cart abandonment. It was built for a 90-second read by leadership ahead of the holiday season.

## Files

| File | What it is |
|---|---|
| `Breaking_Games_Dashboard.html` | The interactive dashboard |
| `Breaking_Games_Dashboard.png` | Full-page screenshot of the dashboard |

## How to View
1. Download `Breaking_Games_Dashboard.html`
2. Double-click it to open it in any browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari)
3. Stay connected to the internet. The charts and styling load from Chart.js and Tailwind CDNs, so offline the page shows text but no charts.

## What's on the Dashboard
- **5 KPI cards:** the numbers leadership needs for Q4 decisions
- **Top 10 Products by Revenue:** units sold and average selling price per unit
- **Revenue Distribution chart:** top 10 products vs. the rest of the catalog
- **Traffic by Channel chart:** pageviews by marketing channel (bot traffic excluded)
- **Key Findings and Recommendations:** three of each

## KPIs

| KPI | Value | What it tells the team |
|---|---|---|
| Total Revenue | $159,612 | Baseline for Q4 targets (Shopify website sales only) |
| ★ Meta vs. Organic Search Conversion | 0.22% vs. 0.50% | Our only paid channel converts at less than half the rate of free search traffic |
| Meta Ad Spend | $98,543 | The budget the Q4 ad decision is about |
| Cart Abandonment (Adjusted) | 26.4% (naive 92.3%) | Checkout isn't broken; the alarming number came from mismatched dates and bot carts |
| Top Product Share of Revenue | 17.7% | One product earns almost a fifth of revenue |

★ = custom KPI I chose beyond the standard defaults.

## Data Behind It
Every number comes from three objects in my SQLite database:

| Object | Type | Feeds |
|---|---|---|
| `dashboard_metrics` | Table | The 5 KPI cards |
| `dashboard_leaderboard` | Table | The top 10 products table |
| `dashboard_channels` | View | The traffic by channel chart |

Numbers were copied into the HTML by hand. To refresh them, rebuild the three objects in SQLite and update the values in the file.

## Tools
SQLite · SQL · HTML · Chart.js · Tailwind CSS

## Data Note
Data is current as of each export: Shopify orders through Aug 31, 2026; Meta through Sep 7, 2026; checkouts through Oct 6, 2026. Shopify direct-to-consumer sales only.
